    "result_text": "All changes compile cleanly and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and reworked the household rules around it. The change touched five small units, each keeping its single responsibility:\n\n**`HouseholdMatcher`** \u2014 Now derives the household key from `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (previously last name + normalized address). `householdId(...)` returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over that key, and `findMembers(...)` groups by the same key \u2014 so duplicate detection keys off the computed household. Dropped the now-unused `AddressNormalizer` dependency (still used by `OwnerFieldsValidator`).\n\n**`HouseholdAssigner`** \u2014 Simplified to just tag the candidate with its deterministic `householdId`. The old back-fill/save-members logic is gone: since the id is derived purely from fields, every household member computes the same value independently, so there's nothing to link. Dropped its `ClinicService` dependency.\n\n**`HouseholdDuplicateChecker`** \u2014 Unchanged logic (delegates to `findMembers`); doc updated to say \"last name and postcode.\"\n\n**`PossibleDuplicateAssigner`** \u2014 `assign` now takes a `declaredHouseholdMember` flag; a declared member is left unflagged rather than run through the soft-match (a declared member is not a suspected duplicate).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Reordered the flow:\n1. Always assign the deterministic `householdId`.\n2. If it's a household duplicate **and** `sharesHousehold` is not set \u2192 **409**.\n3. `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses that block (it no longer creates the link).\n4. A declared member (`householdDuplicate && sharesHousehold`) is passed to the possible-duplicate assigner so it isn't flagged.\n\n`HouseholdSizeAssigner` already keys off `owner.getHouseholdId()`, which is now always the computed value, so the household-size input to membership stays consistent \u2014 no change needed there.\n\nThe existing acceptance test (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) passes: same last name + postcode share a `householdId` (with `sharesHousehold` bypassing the new 409), and a different last name yields a different one.",
